4.@SpringBootApplication – What it does?

	1. JVM starts
	Loads the Main class and executes main()

	2. SpringApplication.run()
	Bootstraps the Spring Boot application

	3. Environment preparation
	Loads properties, profiles and configuration

	4. ApplicationContext creation
	Creates the Spring IoC container

	5. Bean definitions and auto-configuration
	Discovers components and registers bean definitions

	6. Bean creation and dependency injection
	Creates objects, injects dependencies and initializes beans

	7. Embedded server starts
	Tomcat starts for a typical Spring MVC web application

	8. Application ready
	Startup callbacks complete; application can handle requests

