Scopes in Bean:
	singleton 
	- default : singleton project starting itself bean will be create so it called eager initalisation using Constuctor and the same address will be created when api called
	- whenever needed if create bean then it is called lazy initalisation
	- one bean is created and it is resued
	- if we create three bean using autowired then the 3 bean ref will be same
	- if we have a 3 autowired then 1 object will be created everytime it called according to the obj ref **
	- bean is created when needed
	- All three references point to the same singleton object.
		
	prototype 
		- new instance will be created evry time the hascode will be different
		- if the controller and the service have mentioned at prototype then evry time all the autowired will be created new ref 
		- if we have a 3 autowired then 3 object will be created everytime it called **
		
	request  
		- for every api call one instance will be created [SingleTon but every obj will be diff]
	
	session
		- for One complete session same ref Obj will be used
		- for a session multiple api calls can have same obj
		- for diff address diff ref will be created
		- if session and singleton is mixed then error will come at startup Unsatified Dependency Exception
		- we can use the proxyMode = scopedProxyMode.TARGETCLASS
		
