JWT Token:
		
	- without JWT hardcoded values need to pass on the req which is not recommend
	
	- the user need to send the userName and pwd for the 1st time for getting the JWT token and after that user can use the JWT for all the req
	
	- Header Payload Signarture
	
		- Header : Algo and Type
		
		- Payload : DATA 
		
		- signature : expirt time  and encoded 
		
	-Security Level - encription key - 128 bit 256 bit*
		
	- Jwts.builder()
		.setClaims(claims)
		.setSubject(userName)
		.setIssuedAt(new Date(System.currentTimeMillis()))
		.setExpiration(new Date(System.currentTimeMillis()+1000*60*30))
		.signWith(getSignKey(),SignatureAlgorithm.HS256().compact())
	
	Refresh Token :
	
		- JWT will have expiration so after exp user need to ReAuthenticate with username pwd and again need to generate JWT token
		- so Referesh Tokeen can be used instead of ReAuthenticate
		- we can send a refersh token with JSON and get the Token again without the user name and pwd
		
		
	
